SUMMARY:AYPROS x Bounty & Soul: Market Support Volunteer Day 
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Young Professionals (AYPROS)\n**Help us make a diffe
 rence in our community\, one market day at a time!**\n\nJoin AYPROS for an
  afternoon of volunteering with Bounty & Soul in Black Mountain!\n\nWe'll 
 be helping out at Bounty & Soul's Bi-Lo Market\, where volunteers play an 
 important role in keeping things organized\, welcoming\, and running smoot
 hly for community members.\n\nFrom distributing available food and other i
 tems to helping participants carry things to their vehicles\, there are pl
 enty of ways to lend a hand.\n\nNo special experience needed! Just bring a
  willingness to help\, a friendly attitude\, and some comfortable shoes.\n
 \n## Event Details\n\n* **Date:** Thursday\, November 19\, 2026\n* **Time:
 ** 3:00–5:30 PM\n* **Location:** Bounty & Soul Bi-Lo Market\, 205 NC-9\,
  Black Mountain\, NC\n* **Registration:** Free \\| Limited to 12 volunteer
 s\n\n## What We'll Be Doing\n\nOur group will help Bounty & Soul staff wit
 h a variety of market support tasks\, including:\n\n* Distributing availab
 le items to market participants\n* Helping participants understand quantit
 ies and keeping items organized\n* Making sure the market stays welcoming 
 and runs smoothly\n* Assisting participants with carrying items to their v
 ehicles when needed\n* Helping with other tasks depending on the market's 
 needs\n\nIt's a hands-on opportunity to support a local nonprofit while sp
 ending an afternoon giving back alongside fellow young professionals.\n\n#
 # What to Know Before You Go\n\n* **Arrival:** Please arrive on time and c
 heck in with Bounty & Soul staff at the trucks when you arrive.\n* **Waive
 rs:** All volunteers must complete Bounty & Soul's liability waiver before
  participating. You can [\\[download the volunteer waiver here\\]](https:/
 /aypros.wildapricot.org/resources/Bounty%20and%20Soul%20Liability%20Waiver
 %20and%20Photo%20Release.pdf) and bring the completed form with you\, or f
 ill one out on-site.\n* **What to wear:** Closed-toe shoes and shirts with
  sleeves are required. Appropriate shorts or jeans are fine.\n* **Weather:
 ** This is an outdoor market\, so dress for the conditions. The event may 
 take place in sunshine\, cooler temperatures\, or light rain.\n* **Physica
 l activity:** Expect standing and walking throughout the shift\, with some
  light to moderate lifting. Volunteers can decline tasks they aren't physi
 cally comfortable performing.\n* **Age requirements:** Volunteers must be 
 at least 16 to participate independently. Ages 14–15 may volunteer with 
 an adult.\n\n## Why It Matters\n\nBounty & Soul relies on volunteers to he
 lp create a welcoming\, organized market experience for the people it serv
 es.\n\nBy helping with the day-to-day operations\, we're supporting the or
 ganization's work and making it easier for community members to access ava
 ilable food and other resources.\n\nWhether you're a regular AYPROS volunt
 eer or joining us for the first time\, we'd love to have you!\n\n**Only 12
  volunteer spots are available\, so please register in advance to join us!
 **\n\nCome spend an afternoon doing something good for our neighbors and c
 onnecting with fellow young professionals along the way.\n\n### Need Help 
 Finding Us?\n\nIf you have trouble locating the group or are running a few
  minutes behind\, call or text AYPROS Crew Leader **Danielle Klein** at **
 239-287-8952**.\n\n## About AYPROS Leadership & Service\n\nAt AYPROS\, lea
 dership is not only about titles. It is about stepping forward\, showing u
 p\, and doing work that matters.\nOur Leadership & Service events give you
 ng professionals the opportunity to work alongside local organizations add
 ressing real needs across Asheville and Western North Carolina. This clean
 up is a chance to serve the community\, care for the French Broad River\, 
 and get to know others who want to make Asheville stronger.
